your attitude towards failure can  literally change your life  so today i'm going to give you five  reasons that failure can be a good thing  and if you stick to the end you will get  my three tips on helping you to overcome  the fear of failure  reason number one why failure can be  great for you is it can help you  overcome your fears  when i had just started driving i  actually drove into  someone's house i mean the hood of the  car was literally inside the living room  and no i don't have pictures i was not  about to show the world  what i had just done but this experience  this  failure left me feeling like i was a  horrible driver it left me kind of  traumatized and from then on in my mind  i was  always a horrible driver when my husband  and i moved houses  he forced me to move a trailer with our  furniture inside it  me the person who had wrecked a house  i was certain that this was a wreck  waiting to happen  but to my surprise i actually did it  everything got home okay maybe a few  dents in it but nobody was hurt  all the furniture made it i did it when  my husband and i cleared land for a  house build  he taught me how to drive an excavator i  was horrified i thought i was going to  kill myself yes when i drove an  excavator i took twice as long and i  probably did it very wrong in the  beginning  yes when i drove a trailer i did some of  our furniture  but these failures helped me to conquer  the biggest fear that i was having that  fear  of being a horrible driver reason number  two that failure can be great is it can  help you become a better  problem solver what how can making  mistakes make you better at solving  problems  because failure forces you to come up  with new solutions and approaches to  problems that you're not able to solve  i love thomas edison's famous words i  have not  failed i've just found 10 000 ways that  don't work so if studying the same way  keeps resulting in failing grades  maybe you just need to study differently  maybe you need a tutor maybe you need a  study group  maybe you're not an auditory learner  you're a visual learner or vice versa  sometimes failure means that you need to  change direction  not stop and quit altogether we've  learned from darwin that those who adapt  to changes and struggles are those who  come out on top  so when you want to stop when you want  to quit when you feel frustrated  when it's hard don't stop adapt  try finding a new way in approaching the  problem  reason number three that failure can be  awesome is that failure can teach you  persistence  i love the analogy that tony robbins  uses to describe  failure when a child is learning how to  walk a parent just doesn't give him  x number of tries and if they fail  that's it that kid's not gonna walk  no they keep falling and keep falling  and keep trying again  until they learn to walk kids are just  naturally persistent  especially when they want something but  what happens as we  age why is it that we stop trying for  something  once we failed could it be that you've  let  others expectations of you weigh you  down  or could it even be your own  expectations  that you haven't lived up to that is  making you feel like a failure  reason number four is it can help you  become a resource  to other people who are going through  the same kinds of struggles and  hardships that you are  or have been and it kind of makes you  more relatable as well  this can be one of the most difficult  because to let someone see who you  really are  you have to let them see the ugly side  too your failures  but to do this it involves a sense of  vulnerability i find it very  inspirational how oprah winfrey  mentioned on an interview  that she noticed her audience become  dramatically more engaged and willing to  open up  once she first opened up about her own  life  and her struggles she went through major  struggles and had several failures but  she didn't let them stop her  and rather she actually used them to  help other people experiencing failure  which made her more valuable and more  relatable because she became a resource  to other people  your failures might suck but they might  just give you the knowledge and wisdom  to help you accomplish the things that  you thought were not possible  reason number five is it can help you  develop self-awareness  in order to improve at something we  first have to analyze what went wrong in  the first place  but how often do we face a problem and  our first instinct is  but it's not my fault when my toddler  grabbed a basket of eggs from the  kitchen table  broke them and smeared them all over the  floor i could have been upset by what  she did  but who put the eggs within her reach  when you have  a failure don't blame others your  situation or the economy  instead ask yourself what could i have  done differently  you don't have to live life seeing  yourself as a victim  yes you will have failures pains and  disappointments  but you are greater than your  circumstances  acknowledge your mistakes and own up to  them the ability to do this can help you  prevent  possible failures in the future and it  can help you to accomplish  greater things in my video seven lessons  i've learned from working with dying  patients  i mentioned that failure is not  something to fear but something to  pursue  this is because failure is where we  learn grow and adapt  successful people fail a lot but they  learn from it  so now that we've talked about why  failure can be a good thing  let's talk about how to overcome the  fear failure because for some people  just the fear alone is what stops them  from even trying in the first place  so tip number one hang with the wolves  my husband loves to say if you hang with  the wolves you'll learn how to howl  i love my father dearly but when i was a  child he taught me that a  woman could not do the things that men  could i would try to help him  by working on the yard or try to help  him fix things around the house and  actually learn from him  but he would remind me this isn't for  women go and help your mother in the  kitchen  so at a young age i kind of had it  ingrained in me that i would never  really amount to anything or accomplish  anything major in my life  but by the grace of god i made  relationships with true leaders  who actually pushed me to push myself  even further  and to try new things and not let the  fear of failure defeat me  so attract people in your life who are  positive who crave and hunger success  because these are the people that are  going to keep motivating you  to keep going keep pushing and keep  reaching your limit  and if you don't have anyone that meets  this criteria in your life  then read books listen to podcasts or  watch inspirational youtube videos  you are the average of the five people  you spend the most time with  so find the wolves and hang with them  tip number two learn to separate  yourself from your failures  this one was very difficult for me  because i always had the mentality that  if i  fail then i'm a failure so i was  incredibly prideful and i would actually  rarely acknowledge my mistakes because i  thought that doing so would make me weak  or would make me an actual failure  it's actually quite the contrary to be  able to admit that you have failed  and not feel like a failure requires a  degree of  self-acceptance and vulnerability  because one  you're acknowledging your mistakes and  number two you're allowing other people  to see them  allowing yourself to be vulnerable by  admitting to your mistakes can actually  be very freeing because you don't have  to try to be somebody that you're not  so ingrain in your brain i am not a  failure  i just failed or as thomas edison would  say  just learned one other way to not do it  again  and lastly tip number three push  yourself for yourself  not for other people when i was a kid in  school i won lots of awards and  certificates that never brought me joy  because i pushed myself  in the hopes that maybe if i worked hard  enough my parents would see them and be  proud of me  maybe if i accomplished enough they  would show me the love that i conquered  for  this was detrimental behavior because i  was trying to earn acceptance and earn  love and i was basically giving myself a  worth  based on how others perceived me not how  i perceived myself  but i remember my college graduation day  when my family was complaining and  frustrated because they had to drive  three hours  to get there i truthfully didn't care if  they attended or not because  this was about me this time i had done  it and i did not do it for them  there's a whole different feeling and  satisfaction that you get when you  accomplish things  and strive hard for the things that you  want to accomplish  not for what others are wanting you to  achieve or what others are expecting  from you  so those are my three tips to help you  conquer the fear of failure  if you have any more please leave them  in the comments and if you like this  video please give it a thumbs up and  subscribe so that you won't miss out on  my weekly videos  i thank you so much for watching and i  can't wait to see you in the next one

